I wrote all of WP-4. Only the new files and their tests are in the repo. Every edit to an existing server file was refused by the Change Impact hook. That includes edits to my own new service file once it existed: the Write that created it went through, but every later Edit to it was refused.

IN THE REPO:
(1) src/server/services/CompanyYappchattService.ts (new). It holds every rule:
- create-or-link from companies.contactemail, then group creation with the seat limit;
- both ids stored in one conditional update, only after both YappChatt calls succeed (FR-011);
- membership sync: company users get admin (ADMIN) or member; consulting members get member when they have an active subassignment, a current engagementassignment and an active engagement on one of the company's projects;
- each person's YappChatt id is stored; people who are no longer entitled are removed from the group and from every company-owned room; each room gets only its own project's consultants;
- seat_limit_reached is returned in failed[] and logged;
- ensureCompanyRoom: 409 no_company_account { contactEmail } unless createCompanyAccount, sync on every connect, a non-company or ownerless room is retired (C1.9) and replaced, the agent token is minted with the company account's session, owneryappchattid is recorded;
- the Room Approver check;
- a companyauditlogs row for every state change and every decision accepted or refused;
- a Drizzle store and a broker client behind interfaces, so the rules unit-test without a database;
- yappchattSyncObserver, which runs the sync after a successful user or engagement change.
(2) src/server/routes/companyYappchatt.ts (new): GET and POST /api/company/yappchatt per C3. The company comes from the JWT. POST uses requireAdmin and accepts only { confirm: true }. It returns 503 companion_unavailable, 400 invalid_email, and 502 for other YappChatt refusals.
(3) Tests: tests/unit/companyYappchattService.test.ts, tests/unit/yappchattSyncObserver.test.ts, tests/backend/companyYappchatt.route.test.ts.
(4) tests/backend/projectAgent.route.test.ts: added a mock of CompanyYappchattService, so the suite never loads the real db client once projectAgent.ts imports the service.

HOOK-GATED, NOT IN THE REPO: the full intended files are in E:/Temp/claude/e--AI-Development-wxperts-wxKanban/8a6149c7-dd42-4b2a-a562-f0756fa7598d/scratchpad/wp4-pending-edits/:
- yappchattBroker.ts (T005: the C1 client and companion_unavailable);
- CompanyYappchattService.ts (a corrected copy of the repo file);
- AgentConnectService.ts (T008: resolveRoom delegates to ensureCompanyRoom; the room is resolved before the MCP token on the KAIN path; AgentConnectError gains extra fields; the room result gains ownerYappchattId and replacedConversationId);
- projectAgent.ts (createCompanyAccount, 409 { contactEmail }, 503, and the T009 GET /approver route);
