- app.ts (mounts the sync observer, and /api/company/yappchatt before companyRoutes).
Each comes with a .patch file against the original and a .orig.ts snapshot, plus tests/ with two pending test files.

Two defects stay in the repo copy of CompanyYappchattService.ts until the corrected copy replaces it:
(a) The fences are nested inside the class, so auditfences reports UNFENCED_DECL for class CompanyYappchattService at line 247.
(b) seatLimit orders companysubscriptions ascending, so it reads the oldest active or trialing row instead of the newest.
The corrected copy also changes the room loop so that one failing member no longer skips the rest of that room.

Why the observer instead of editing the user and engagement routes: team.ts, engagements.ts, InvitationService.ts and EngagementModificationQueue.ts still match the legacy fence baseline. Editing them would turn every unfenced route in them into an auditfences error, and they are not in my ownership list. One line mounted in app.ts covers all of these paths after the response is sent, so the sync can never block or fail those flows.

