handoffs.summary:
I made all five doc changes. No production code was touched and no Change Impact hook denied anything.

1. docs/kain-contract.md
- New note at the top: what SPEC-144 changes for KAIN, and that none of it is live until SPEC-144 and YappChatt SPEC-093 ship.
- Section 1: the project MCP token is also the Bearer for the room read login. A retired room takes no new posts.
- Section 3: the connect reply now carries `room.ownerYappchattId` and `room.replacedConversationId`. Two new errors: 409 `no_company_account` with `{contactEmail}` (no room is created, and KAIN cannot create the account), and 503 `companion_unavailable`.
- Section 3 also explains who owns a room: the company account. Members are all company users plus the consultants on that project, kept in sync. Old rooms are retired and replaced, and KAIN must switch to the new `conversationId`.
- Section 4: `/api/community/session` now needs `Authorization: Bearer <project MCP token>`. The email must be a company user or a consulting member assigned to one of its projects. The section lists the answers: 401 `token_required`, 401 `invalid-token`, and 403 `not_company_member` with "This email isn't a member of your company" (the refusal is audited).
- Sections 5 and 7: "owner" now means Room Approver (an ADMIN, or a TEAM_MANAGER who is a current member of the project). Approvers' answers and reviews are recorded under their own name. Anyone else's reply is treated as discussion and gets the "Not recorded: only an ADMIN or this project's TEAM_MANAGER can decide." note. KAIN still never reviews.

2. docs-workspace/sections/process-decision-memory.md, "When KAIN answers for you": only Room Approvers decide (Admin, or a Manager who is on the project, matching the role labels on the Team Members page). Decisions are recorded under their name. Other replies are not recorded and the room says so. Reviews are recorded under the approver's name. Added a link to the new Team chat section and SPEC-144 to `sources`.

3. New help section docs-workspace/sections/team-chat.md. It follows the existing section format and describes the panel WP-5 built (Settings, Company tab, under Agent Access). It covers:
- what the panel shows, including the "isn't ready" message;
- creating the account from the contact email (the Billing Email field), what happens for a new account, an existing one, or a second press;
- who is in the group and in each room;
- automatic sync, and that changes made by hand in YappChatt are undone at the next sync;
- room naming, the no-account offer, and retired rooms;
- Room Approvers, the Community Help gate, and the audit log.
I added "team-chat" after "team" in config.json group "3C. Company admins". I did not add it to `section_order`, which only lists screens that have their own capture. The only email in the text is an example.com one, so the manual's leak scan stays clean.

4. specs/142-decision-memory/spec.md, Amendment A FR-021: added one note saying SCOPE-144 / SPEC-144 FR-008 replaces "a human post is the owner" with Room Approvers, checked through `GET /api/project-agent/approver` and recorded with the approver's name as `approved_by`.

5. New specs/144-company-yappchatt-account/acceptance.md, the T015 live plan. Every row is marked "not run". It contains:
- preconditions P1 to P6: SPEC-093 deployed, SQL applied with its VERIFY block and db:drift, SPEC-144 deployed, the shared secret matching, the fixture in place, and the bridge release installed;
- a test fixture: Acme Test with 5 users (A1 ADMIN, M1 TEAM_MANAGER on Billing, U1 to U3), projects Billing and Payroll, a consulting firm with C1 on Billing and C2 on Payroll, plus Other Test, NoChat Test and an outsider;
- read-only queries for wxKanban (T1 to T4) and for the YappChatt schema (Y1 to Y4);
- step tables for US1 to US6 and SC1 to SC7, each saying exactly what to check in the data;
- extra checks E1 to E3: companion missing, a hand-made membership change undone, seat limit reported;
- two open questions to settle before the run.
